```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the CRC functionality is being accessed while the display power is off, which is indicated by the first code statement. This leads to an error when trying to capture CRC data. Additionally, enabling the Intelligent Power Saving (IPS) feature without ensuring that the display is powered on can lead to improper CRC functionality, as the IPS may interfere with the CRC operations.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (!source) {
    ...
    hsw_enable_ips(intel_crtc);
}
```
Reason:
The fix involves ensuring that the IPS is only enabled when the source is valid and the display is powered on. This prevents the situation where the CRC is captured while the display is off, thus ensuring that the CRC functionality works correctly in conjunction with the IPS feature. The removal of the direct call to `hsw_enable_ips(intel_crtc);` when the source is not set helps to avoid the unintended interaction that caused the original bug.

